WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.282 --> 00:00:01.882
- I just think that she's finding it

00:00:01.882 --> 00:00:04.664
hard to understand why someone like me

00:00:04.664 --> 00:00:06.916
would vote for someone like him, right?

00:00:06.916 --> 00:00:07.930
- Yes. (laughing)

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:09.010
- It's hard, it's weird.

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:09.941
I don't know how to explain it.

00:00:09.941 --> 00:00:11.281
Don't look at me with your killing eyes.

00:00:11.281 --> 00:00:13.041
(laughing)

00:00:13.041 --> 00:00:14.960
(whooshing and squeeking)

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.364
(light guitar music)

00:00:17.364 --> 00:00:19.458
- My name is Kelsey and I
voted for Hillary Clinton.

00:00:19.458 --> 00:00:22.030
Today, I came here with Dean
and Dean is my neighbor.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.475
- I was in the United States Army,

00:00:23.475 --> 00:00:26.376
and I served for five years
and I voted for Donald Trump.

00:00:26.376 --> 00:00:28.623
- My name is Vanessa
and I voted for Hillary.

00:00:28.623 --> 00:00:30.977
I'm here today with my boyfriend Jose.

00:00:30.977 --> 00:00:32.745
- I voted for Donald Trump.

00:00:32.745 --> 00:00:34.370
- So we're here to talk
about Hillary and Donald.

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:35.203
- Oh Donald.

00:00:35.203 --> 00:00:36.036
- Yeah.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:36.869
- What a guy.

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:37.796
- Yeah he's your guy.

00:00:37.796 --> 00:00:39.592
- Well you know.
(laughing)

00:00:39.592 --> 00:00:40.425
He's a guy, you know, he's a guy.

00:00:40.425 --> 00:00:42.324
The decision to vote
for Trump was probably

00:00:42.324 --> 00:00:44.508
the most difficult voting
decision I've ever made

00:00:44.508 --> 00:00:45.430
in my entire life.

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:47.548
I don't like Trump as a human being.

00:00:47.548 --> 00:00:50.444
I didn't make my actual decision
on who to vote for really

00:00:50.444 --> 00:00:52.212
until the day of.

00:00:52.212 --> 00:00:53.816
I didn't sleep that night.

00:00:53.816 --> 00:00:55.206
- What made you vote for Trump

00:00:55.206 --> 00:00:57.546
after we were oh yay for Hillary.

00:00:57.546 --> 00:01:00.740
I felt really great going in
that day voting for Hillary.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.144
We needed the change,

00:01:02.144 --> 00:01:03.718
and needed some woman power there.

00:01:03.718 --> 00:01:06.062
When I found out my
boyfriend had voted for Trump

00:01:06.062 --> 00:01:07.816
I was extremely pissed.

00:01:07.816 --> 00:01:10.160
- I told you the whole
shebang about like, you know,

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.032
what I know about him and ...

00:01:12.032 --> 00:01:12.865
- All you read was,

00:01:12.865 --> 00:01:14.616
or you watched a documentary. (laughing)

00:01:14.616 --> 00:01:16.124
- No, she thinks I only
watched a documentary.

00:01:16.124 --> 00:01:19.074
I knew so much more
before the documentary.

00:01:19.074 --> 00:01:21.455
I decided to vote for Donald Trump

00:01:21.455 --> 00:01:26.031
because he has a new,
fresh eye into politics.

00:01:26.031 --> 00:01:28.226
He actually cares for this country

00:01:28.226 --> 00:01:29.577
because he's like a super American.

00:01:29.577 --> 00:01:31.034
He's like more proud of America

00:01:31.034 --> 00:01:32.687
than he is of anything in the world.

00:01:32.687 --> 00:01:34.545
Vanessa and I kind of talked about it,

00:01:34.545 --> 00:01:36.546
but I kind of lied.

00:01:36.546 --> 00:01:39.834
- He didn't tell me at all
who he voted for at the booth.

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:42.803
- I was trying to avoid argument.

00:01:42.803 --> 00:01:45.413
- I had to find out when
he was a little bit tipsy

00:01:45.413 --> 00:01:46.503
when we were with our friends

00:01:46.503 --> 00:01:47.885
that he actually voted for Trump.

00:01:47.885 --> 00:01:48.887
I was so hurt.

00:01:48.887 --> 00:01:51.186
- I get that you voted for Trump.

00:01:51.186 --> 00:01:52.825
You cared about his economic plans.

00:01:52.825 --> 00:01:54.711
And the hard thing for
me of what I don't get,

00:01:54.711 --> 00:01:56.176
some of the stuff that he's said

00:01:56.176 --> 00:01:57.675
when it came to like women,

00:01:57.675 --> 00:01:59.974
or when it came to just
like other groups of people.

00:01:59.974 --> 00:02:02.002
- I've never been a woman in America.

00:02:02.002 --> 00:02:03.233
I couldn't tell you not to be offended

00:02:03.233 --> 00:02:04.446
by the things that he's said.

00:02:04.446 --> 00:02:06.356
Kelsey and I are similar in a lot of ways

00:02:06.356 --> 00:02:07.618
but different in a lot of ways.

00:02:07.618 --> 00:02:08.620
She's from the mid-west.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:09.854
I'm actually from New York,

00:02:09.854 --> 00:02:11.660
but I lived in Texas for seven years.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.026
I don't like his rhetoric,

00:02:13.026 --> 00:02:15.248
I don't like the things
that he said about women,

00:02:15.248 --> 00:02:17.134
but you never agree
with 100% of everything

00:02:17.134 --> 00:02:18.459
that your candidate believes.

00:02:18.459 --> 00:02:19.995
- I mean there are policies
that Bush or Romney

00:02:19.995 --> 00:02:22.064
or, you know, McCain suggested,

00:02:22.064 --> 00:02:24.092
that I wasn't necessarily on board with,

00:02:24.092 --> 00:02:25.819
but I didn't feel offended by them.

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:28.473
That's what's different about this one.

00:02:28.473 --> 00:02:29.368
- Completely understand that.

00:02:29.368 --> 00:02:31.814
- What you don't understand
is that he's a celebrity.

00:02:31.814 --> 00:02:33.029
So he's gonna like say things.

00:02:33.029 --> 00:02:37.352
- That's why he shouldn't
be on the poll. (laughing)

00:02:37.352 --> 00:02:38.808
- Listen to me, listen.

00:02:38.808 --> 00:02:40.732
She's so confident in
what she believes in.

00:02:40.732 --> 00:02:42.604
She's like really, like on it.

00:02:42.604 --> 00:02:44.126
- All I know is Trump is not good.

00:02:44.126 --> 00:02:46.556
- You only think he's not
good because of what he said.

00:02:46.556 --> 00:02:47.622
- They were talking about Hispanics

00:02:47.622 --> 00:02:49.122
and how he's so racist and everything,

00:02:49.122 --> 00:02:50.550
and we're Hispanic.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:51.516
He meant every word.

00:02:51.516 --> 00:02:52.578
- I don't think so.

00:02:52.578 --> 00:02:54.806
I know that he did make, you know,

00:02:54.806 --> 00:02:56.478
some comments that were not,

00:02:56.478 --> 00:02:57.378
they weren't nice,

00:02:57.378 --> 00:02:59.174
but I'm very open-minded.

00:02:59.174 --> 00:03:00.274
I was laughing about it.

00:03:00.274 --> 00:03:03.216
I was like, this guy is so
dumb, he's just a celebrity.

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:07.086
He says like certain things
in order to create ratings

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:09.220
and in order to create suspense.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:11.966
- My friends are like getting
harassed because of Trump.

00:03:11.966 --> 00:03:13.408
- You know I would never do that.

00:03:13.408 --> 00:03:15.890
I mean I wouldn't talk to people
the way he talks to people.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.010
- I don't like Hillary.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.152
The fact that she's done some
of the things that she's done.

00:03:19.152 --> 00:03:20.660
The emails on her private server.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.598
I mean let's not pretend
like that's not a big deal.

00:03:22.598 --> 00:03:24.196
- I volunteered for her in Los Angeles.

00:03:24.196 --> 00:03:26.720
She seemed like somebody
who was going to keep

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:27.938
progressing us forward,

00:03:27.938 --> 00:03:29.498
especially in terms of social issues.

00:03:29.498 --> 00:03:30.852
I totally get where you're coming from

00:03:30.852 --> 00:03:32.306
'cause you have that military experience

00:03:32.306 --> 00:03:33.764
and that's why I like to
talk to you about stuff.

00:03:33.764 --> 00:03:35.262
And he says to John McCain,

00:03:35.262 --> 00:03:36.742
"Oh I like people who don't get caught."

00:03:36.742 --> 00:03:38.338
I'm like, is this the man that like,

00:03:38.338 --> 00:03:40.046
the Republican Party believes is like

00:03:40.046 --> 00:03:41.294
the best representative?

00:03:41.294 --> 00:03:42.736
- I mean obviously I was frustrated too.

00:03:42.736 --> 00:03:43.592
The thing for me.

00:03:43.592 --> 00:03:45.908
It just went so farther
beyond like all the rhetoric

00:03:45.908 --> 00:03:47.364
that was coming out of both sides

00:03:47.364 --> 00:03:50.240
and I just did my best
to try to see past that

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.480
and see what I thought
the republican America

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.339
would look like over the
next four to eight years

00:03:54.339 --> 00:03:56.914
as opposed to what the
Democratic Hillary Clinton

00:03:56.914 --> 00:03:58.176
America would look like.

00:03:58.176 --> 00:03:59.306
- It is hard because even now,

00:03:59.306 --> 00:04:01.409
like, they even say, he doesn't
even know what he's doing

00:04:01.409 --> 00:04:02.369
on the chair.

00:04:02.369 --> 00:04:04.559
Like, he didn't know what
he was getting himself into.

00:04:04.559 --> 00:04:06.159
And like he's just a mess.

00:04:06.159 --> 00:04:07.668
She knew everything.

00:04:07.668 --> 00:04:08.900
He knows nothing.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:11.049
- Could you give me almost any other woman

00:04:11.049 --> 00:04:11.882
who was qualified.

00:04:11.882 --> 00:04:13.489
I would have been much more open

00:04:13.489 --> 00:04:14.866
to having that discussion.

00:04:14.866 --> 00:04:16.340
I'm not saying Hillary
needs to be in prison.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.173
I'm not gonna run around

00:04:17.173 --> 00:04:18.426
with a Hillary for Prison
sticker on my truck.

00:04:18.426 --> 00:04:19.259
You know that I won't.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:21.403
- For me to talk to him from
the perspective of, you know,

00:04:21.403 --> 00:04:23.855
being a female might help
him learn about issues

00:04:23.855 --> 00:04:26.186
with women's health
and with women's rights

00:04:26.186 --> 00:04:27.993
that, you know, maybe just
aren't something he thinks about

00:04:27.993 --> 00:04:29.142
in his day to day life.

00:04:29.142 --> 00:04:31.108
I do think for a lot of
people, myself included,

00:04:31.108 --> 00:04:34.110
I did not vote for Hillary
Clinton because she was a woman,

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:37.948
but it definitely seemed like
she understood women's issues

00:04:37.948 --> 00:04:39.068
a lot more than Donald.

00:04:39.068 --> 00:04:40.531
Even just on a policy level.

00:04:40.531 --> 00:04:42.742
- What you're saying is like
'cause women are just nervous

00:04:42.742 --> 00:04:45.720
that Trump is gonna roll back rights.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.662
- Well, so if you want to
hear what I'm concerned about

00:04:47.662 --> 00:04:49.072
like in terms of women's issues.

00:04:49.072 --> 00:04:51.782
Some different aspects that
were covered by Obamacare

00:04:51.782 --> 00:04:53.123
potentially would be rolled back

00:04:53.123 --> 00:04:55.302
and then as far as like, you know,

00:04:55.302 --> 00:04:56.902
the supreme court justice picks,

00:04:56.902 --> 00:05:00.540
admitted that he would be
comfortable with electing people

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:03.020
who were okay with
overturning Roe v. Wade.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:03.853
- I'm a republican.

00:05:03.853 --> 00:05:05.422
I identify with republicans.

00:05:05.422 --> 00:05:07.740
I do tend to lean more
toward like the middle.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.854
At the end of the day I had
to align myself with my party

00:05:09.854 --> 00:05:10.740
and have faith that

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.494
they're not gonna let him do crazy things

00:05:12.494 --> 00:05:13.580
when he's in office.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.174
As far as the supreme court
justices and the Roe v. Wade,

00:05:15.174 --> 00:05:18.672
that's (exhaling).

00:05:18.672 --> 00:05:19.505
I can't,

00:05:19.505 --> 00:05:22.414
as a guy, I can't tell you
not to be worried about that

00:05:22.414 --> 00:05:23.247
or how to feel.

00:05:23.247 --> 00:05:25.894
I don't even think I could
possibly understand how you feel.

00:05:25.894 --> 00:05:26.727
- Yeah.

00:05:26.727 --> 00:05:27.683
It's like scary.

00:05:27.683 --> 00:05:29.740
- Yeah that's one of those things,

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:31.883
I mean I can just kind of be
a friend and be there for you.

00:05:31.883 --> 00:05:33.323
- She knows who I am

00:05:33.323 --> 00:05:36.500
and she knows that ultimately
if I made a mistake

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.860
or if something like bad is happening,

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:43.134
I will do whatever I can
to help the situation.

00:05:43.134 --> 00:05:44.822
- I'm glad that we get
to get it off our chest.

00:05:44.822 --> 00:05:46.580
I do know, Jose, the way you say.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:47.912
It's just that little like,

00:05:47.912 --> 00:05:50.380
like that little one little percenter.

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.182
You like question, like what wait,

00:05:52.182 --> 00:05:54.392
what the puck is going on over here.

00:05:54.392 --> 00:05:55.912
- If there was something crazy happening,

00:05:55.912 --> 00:05:57.152
you were put at risk,

00:05:57.152 --> 00:05:59.222
like I would be the first one
standing there next to you

00:05:59.222 --> 00:06:01.043
to fight that same battle with you.

00:06:01.043 --> 00:06:02.420
Because equality matters,

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:03.974
like rights, human rights matter.

00:06:03.974 --> 00:06:06.262
- I never said that I
didn't agree that, you know,

00:06:06.262 --> 00:06:08.020
he's cocky, arrogant.

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:09.574
But I said at least, you know,

00:06:09.574 --> 00:06:11.414
since it's already happening, you know,

00:06:11.414 --> 00:06:13.621
might as well just like go along with it.

00:06:13.621 --> 00:06:15.952
Kind of like when you go to the doctor

00:06:15.952 --> 00:06:17.421
and they tell you you have like cancer

00:06:17.421 --> 00:06:18.814
and you have like six months to live.

00:06:18.814 --> 00:06:19.647
What are you gonna do?

00:06:19.647 --> 00:06:20.480
Like,

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:21.742
the best thing to do is just like

00:06:21.742 --> 00:06:22.860
kind of do the best you can.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:24.672
- If you're somebody who

00:06:24.672 --> 00:06:26.912
felt strongly about
this political election

00:06:26.912 --> 00:06:29.050
and have people that you
care about in your lives

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:31.563
that you want to talk to about it,

00:06:31.563 --> 00:06:34.569
I think it's important to
find out where they came from

00:06:34.569 --> 00:06:36.131
and research their perspective.

00:06:36.131 --> 00:06:37.731
- Voice your opinion for one.

00:06:37.731 --> 00:06:39.603
- We're already in this and
the best thing we can do

00:06:39.603 --> 00:06:41.552
is help each other, support each other.

00:06:41.552 --> 00:06:43.910
I don't really think
it's worth the arguments

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:44.888
and the fights.

00:06:44.888 --> 00:06:46.310
Because at the end of the day,

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:48.059
you're not gonna be
able to change anything.

00:06:48.059 --> 00:06:50.767
The only thing you can
change is your relationship.

00:06:50.767 --> 00:06:52.167
- It's tough to get perspective

00:06:52.167 --> 00:06:54.448
if you don't put yourself
in that environment

00:06:54.448 --> 00:06:55.390
and have those conversations.

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:57.447
You can't be afraid to
have these conversations.

00:06:57.447 --> 00:06:59.847
'Cause conversation is what sparks change.

00:06:59.847 --> 00:07:02.179
When I get to sit down
and so my eyes get opened

00:07:02.179 --> 00:07:04.190
and I get a better perspective of things.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:07.190
It's what drives our nation forward.

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:09.619
She baked a bangin' cake.

00:07:09.619 --> 00:07:10.851
I was about to go and
get some of this cake.

00:07:10.851 --> 00:07:11.977
It had Hillary's face all over it.

00:07:11.977 --> 00:07:13.070
She didn't let me have any of that cake.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:14.051
- 'Cause I ate it all.

00:07:14.051 --> 00:07:15.419
It wasn't 'cause I kept it from you.

00:07:15.419 --> 00:07:18.296
(whooshing and creaking)

